## Active workstream

Greenfield re-establishment of sbt-server from a development hand-off. The
original workspace (three Rust crates: `sbt-server-core`, `sbtd`, `sbtctl`)
was built and live-tested on another machine and handed over as a
five-photo HANDOFF.md, now transcribed verbatim at the project root and
converted into the binding constraints in ARCHITECTURE.md. This checkout
holds only the rules layer: no Cargo workspace, no source, no commits yet.
Binding decisions already made: agents reach `sbtd` over loopback HTTP only;
`sbtd` drives sbt via its own JSON-RPC protocol (not BSP/LSP) through a
transport-generic client; `Instance::start` always takes over a pre-existing
`active.json`; shutdown is bounded; raw stdout/stderr is captured alongside
JSON-RPC notifications; the completion line is synthesized because sbt never
sends its banner to clients. Tracker is GitHub Issues
(`scottweaver/sbt-server`); the GitHub repo does not exist yet.

